    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1501">

                <pb facs="1299" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/587</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Minister in Roumania, Servia, and Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vopicka</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 19, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Your March 4.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1501-f1"/> American Red Cross considering
                    question tents for hospitals. Expects to send in April Red Cross sanitary
                    commission under Dr. Richard P. Strong, professor tropical
                    diseases, <pb facs="1300" n="1042" xml:id="pg1042"/> Harvard University.
                    Commission will carry large stores, disinfecting apparatus, and supplies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
